<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>2.4 Solving the heat equation</title>
  <alert>MTH 401</alert>

<remark>
  <p>
    General steps to solving the heat equation:
    <dl>
      <li>
        <title>Step 1:</title>
        <p>
          Is it a homogeneous equation with homogeneous boundary conditions? If not, make it so.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <title>Step 2:</title>
        <p>
          Separation of variables.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <title>Step 3:</title>
        <p>
          Identify and solve the Sturm-Lioville problem.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <title>Step 4:</title>
        <p>
          Solve temporal differential equation, write product solutions, use superposition to write general solution.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <title>Step 5:</title>
        <p>
          Find Fourier Coefficients.
        </p>
      </li>
    </dl>
  </p>
</remark>

  <introduction>
    <p>Here are some examples of the heat equation along with boundary and
initial conditions.  Find a solution for each and graph it using
Mathematica (recommended, can use other technology).</p>
  </introduction>

   <exercise workspace="3in">
    <statement>
      <p><md>
  \begin{aligned}
    \pd{u}{t} \amp  = 4 \pdtwo{u}{x} \\
    u(0, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(5, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(x, 0) \amp  = 3\sin\left(\frac{\pi x}{5}\right)
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p><md>
  \begin{aligned}
    \pd{u}{t} \amp  = 4 \pdtwo{u}{x} \\
    u(0, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(5, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(x, 0) \amp  = x^2 - 5x
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p><md>
  \begin{aligned}
    \pd{u}{t} \amp  = 4 \pdtwo{u}{x} \\
    \pd{u}{x}(0, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    \pd{u}{x}(5, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(x, 0) \amp  = x
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p><md>
  \begin{aligned}
    \pd{u}{t} \amp  = 4 \pdtwo{u}{x} + 8\\
    u(0, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(5, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(x, 0) \amp  = 5x - x^2 
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="5in">
    <statement>
      <p><md>
  \begin{aligned}
    \pd{u}{t} \amp  = 4 \pdtwo{u}{x} + 8\\
    u(0, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(5, t) \amp  = 0 \\
    u(x, 0) \amp  = 0
  \end{aligned}
  </md></p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
